  "notes": "Scandinavian dance-pop with an R&B-inflected topline. Two claims carry the drums: \"clipped programmed kick and clap, offbeat 8th hats opening to 16ths in the chorus, filtered noise fills\" is the weighted `hihat.base` across 8th and 16th with `riser` percussion standing in for a snare-roll fill, and \"deep-house-derived shuffle on the dance records\" is the one place this model swings — `swing.amount` 0.54 on a 16th grid, which is a reading of the word \"shuffle\" and nothing more. The 808 is authored because the entry names it, but at the weight the entry gives it: \"filtered pumping synth sub; occasional 808 in the R&B-facing verses\", so `bass808` is `counter_riff` with a low slide probability while the pumping synth sub remains the bassline on `offbeat_8ths`. Harmony is \"4-bar minor vamps\" with \"a Max-Martin-school pre-chorus lift to the relative major\", which is why a major family sits alongside the minor ones rather than a modulation being faked. The melody block encodes the school shape the entry names outright — \"narrow verse, ascending pre-chorus with rhythmic acceleration, then a wide-interval chorus stated twice\" — as `long_arc` with an arch contour, a wide `densityPerBar` spread and `twoBarCellRepeat` for the doubled chorus statement; \"a clean, unbreathy tone and a wide chorus leap\" is the raised `octaveJumpProb`. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says the parameters are \"lane-conventional\": every drum probability, `swing.amount`, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 112 (the midpoint of the stated 100—125 band) are INFERRED. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the vocal-tone claim is repeated here.",
